{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s45-p01",
      "text": "What would happen if you tried to blow a soap bubble in below freezing weather?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p02",
      "text": "Would it freeze and fall to the ground?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p03",
      "text": "Would you have to hit it with a stone to break it?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p04",
      "text": "These questions came into my mind one cold winter day as I finished my freshly baked apple pie.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p05",
      "text": "It was a perfect time to experiment with blowing frozen bubbles.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p06-01",
      "text": "To blow frozen bubbles, I had to wait until the air outside was very cold,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p06-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p06-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p06-02",
      "text": "meaning 10 degrees below zero Fahrenheit or colder.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p06-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p06-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p07",
      "text": "I didn't have the bubble things that come in a bottle, so I used dish-washing soap.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p08",
      "text": "I chose a place out of the wind, and blew bubbles the same way I always do.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p09",
      "text": "Here's what I learned.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p10",
      "text": "If the temperature is low enough, the skin of the bubble frosts over, becoming cloudy instead of clear.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p10.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p11",
      "text": "And what about those rainbow swirls that you see in soap bubbles?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p12",
      "text": "The rainbow colours stay even when the bubbles frost, but they don't spin any more.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p13",
      "text": "The bubbles still float in the air.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p14",
      "text": "They don't fall to the ground any faster than they would on a summer day.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p15",
      "text": "When these bubbles break, they don't turn into tiny drops of soap.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p16",
      "text": "They turn into shiny rainbow-coloured pieces and fly slowly to the ground.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p17",
      "text": "Sometimes a frozen bubble will roll across the snow without breaking.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p17.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p17.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s45-p18",
      "text": "If it breaks, it may leave a strong bubble skin on the ground.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p18.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p18.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
